    "summary": "Paul describes the latter-day apostasy—Christ is the Savior of all men, especially of those who believe.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Now the Spirit speaketh expressly, that in the latter times some shall depart from the faith, giving heed to seducing spirits, and doctrines of devils;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "TG Last Days."
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "TG Holy Ghost, Loss of."
          },
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "GR deceitful. TG Apostasy of the Early Christian Church; Spirits, Evil or Unclean."
          },
          {
            "start": 131,
            "end": 150,
            "text": "TG False Doctrine."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Speaking lies in hypocrisy; having their conscience seared with a hot iron;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Lying."
          },
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Hypocrisy."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Conscience; Spiritual Blindness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Forbidding to marry, and commanding to abstain from meats, which God hath created to be received with thanksgiving of them which believe and know the truth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "Matt. 8:14; D&C 49:15. TG Marriage, Temporal."
          },
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Marry."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "TG Abstain."
          },
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "TG Food; Word of Wisdom."
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "D&C 49:19."
          },
          {
            "start": 102,
            "end": 114,
            "text": "D&C 89:11 (11–13)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For every creature of God is good, and nothing to be refused, if it be received with thanksgiving:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "GR creation."
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "Gen. 1:31."
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "TG Thanksgiving."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 28
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For it is sanctified by the word of God and prayer.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If thou put the brethren in remembrance of these things, thou shalt be a good minister of Jesus Christ, nourished up in the words of faith and of good doctrine, whereunto thou hast attained.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 161,
            "end": 189,
            "text": "GR which thou hast followed closely."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But refuse profane and old wives’ fables, and exercise thyself rather unto godliness.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 69
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For bodily exercise profiteth little: but godliness is profitable unto all things, having promise of the life that now is, and of that which is to come.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "GR a little while."
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "Luke 12:31. TG Godliness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "This is a faithful saying and worthy of all acceptation.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For therefore we both labour and suffer reproach, because we trust in the living God, who is the Saviour of all men, specially of those that believe.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "TG Labor."
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "TG Reproach."
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Trust in God."
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Atonement through; Jesus Christ, Savior."
          },
          {
            "start": 141,
            "end": 148,
            "text": "TG Faith."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "These things command and teach.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let no man despise thy youth; but be thou an example of the believers, in word, in conversation, in charity, in spirit, in faith, in purity.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "1 Cor. 16:11 (10–11)."
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Example; Priesthood, Qualifying for."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "GR conduct, behavior."
          },
          {
            "start": 133,
            "end": 139,
            "text": "TG Chastity; Purity; Virtue."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Till I come, give attendance to reading, to exhortation, to doctrine.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "TG Study."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Neglect not the gift that is in thee, which was given thee by prophecy, with the laying on of the hands of the presbytery.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "TG Priesthood, Magnifying Callings within."
          },
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG God, Gifts of; Stewardship; Talents."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "1 Tim. 1:18. TG Prophecy."
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "TG Priesthood, Authority; Priesthood, Ordination."
          },
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "TG Hands, Laying on of."
          },
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 121,
            "text": "GR elders."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Meditate upon these things; give thyself wholly to them; that thy profiting may appear to all.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Meditation."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "GR progress, advancement."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "GR be manifest in all."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Take heed unto thyself, and unto the doctrine; continue in them: for in doing this thou shalt both save thyself, and them that hear thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "James 5:20 (19–20); D&C 101:39 (39–40)."
